    Answers are scored as strings, so an answer the memory already holds is only
    worth what its spelling is worth: a solver that paraphrases it, or that adds
    or drops a conventional word ending, loses a sample it had the evidence to
    win. This class holds the answers as the units they are compared in and
    reports which units of a draft appear in the memory, which are one of its
    answers spelled differently, and which the memory has nothing like.
